Relevant tables / columns and their roles  
• pizza_clean_customer_orders.order_id: connect an order to its pizza, exclusions & extras  
• pizza_clean_customer_orders.pizza_id: tells which pizza was ordered (1 = Meat Lovers, 2 = Vegetarian)  
• pizza_names.pizza_name: lets us read the human name of each pizza (useful for checking id ↔ name)  
• pizza_clean_runner_orders.order_id: connects to delivery information for the same order  
• pizza_clean_runner_orders.cancellation: NULL = delivered; non‑NULL = cancelled (must be excluded)  
• pizza_get_extras.order_id: links a row of extra toppings to its order  
• pizza_get_extras.extras_count: how many extra toppings are on that row (charge $1 each)  

Main conditions  
• pizza_clean_runner_orders.cancellation IS NULL  → keep only completed deliveries  
• pizza_clean_customer_orders.pizza_id IN (1,2)  → the two pizzas we price ($12 & $10)  

Below are ten exploratory → final SQL queries (each LIMITED to 20 rows except the final total).  

```sql
-- 1. Look up the pizza id / name mapping
SELECT DISTINCT "pizza_id", "pizza_name"
FROM "pizza_names"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Inspect runner records that were NOT cancelled
SELECT DISTINCT "order_id", "cancellation"
FROM "pizza_clean_runner_orders"
WHERE "cancellation" IS NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Glance at customers’ raw orders (pizza chosen & any extras string)
SELECT DISTINCT "order_id", "pizza_id", "extras"
FROM "pizza_clean_customer_orders"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. View the per–extra‑row information
SELECT DISTINCT "order_id", "extras", "extras_count"
FROM "pizza_get_extras"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Total extras per order (aggregation step we will reuse)
SELECT "order_id",
       SUM("extras_count") AS total_extras
FROM "pizza_get_extras"
GROUP BY "order_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Orders that were actually delivered, linked with their pizzas
SELECT DISTINCT d."order_id",
       c."pizza_id"
FROM "pizza_clean_runner_orders" AS d
JOIN "pizza_clean_customer_orders" AS c
  ON d."order_id" = c."order_id"
WHERE d."cancellation" IS NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Add the extras count to those delivered orders
SELECT DISTINCT o."order_id",
       o."pizza_id",
       COALESCE(e.total_extras,0) AS total_extras
FROM (
      SELECT d."order_id", c."pizza_id"
      FROM "pizza_clean_runner_orders" d
      JOIN "pizza_clean_customer_orders" c
        ON d."order_id" = c."order_id"
      WHERE d."cancellation" IS NULL
     ) AS o
LEFT JOIN (
            SELECT "order_id",
                   SUM("extras_count") AS total_extras
            FROM "pizza_get_extras"
            GROUP BY "order_id"
          ) AS e
  ON o."order_id" = e."order_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Compute the revenue for each single delivered order
SELECT DISTINCT t."order_id",
       t."pizza_id",
       CASE WHEN t."pizza_id" = 1 THEN 12
            WHEN t."pizza_id" = 2 THEN 10
       END                           AS base_price,
       t.total_extras,
       CASE WHEN t."pizza_id" = 1 THEN 12
            WHEN t."pizza_id" = 2 THEN 10
       END + t.total_extras          AS order_revenue
FROM (
      /* derived table identical to query 7 */
      SELECT o."order_id", o."pizza_id", COALESCE(e.total_extras,0) AS total_extras
      FROM (
            SELECT d."order_id", c."pizza_id"
            FROM "pizza_clean_runner_orders" d
            JOIN "pizza_clean_customer_orders" c
              ON d."order_id" = c."order_id"
            WHERE d."cancellation" IS NULL
           ) AS o
      LEFT JOIN (
                  SELECT "order_id",
                         SUM("extras_count") AS total_extras
                  FROM "pizza_get_extras"
                  GROUP BY "order_id"
                ) AS e
        ON o."order_id" = e."order_id"
     ) AS t
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Check a subtotal grouped by pizza type
SELECT DISTINCT
       CASE WHEN pizza_id = 1 THEN 'Meat Lovers'
            WHEN pizza_id = 2 THEN 'Vegetarian'
       END                    AS pizza_type,
       SUM( CASE WHEN pizza_id = 1 THEN 12
                 WHEN pizza_id = 2 THEN 10
            END + COALESCE(total_extras,0) ) AS revenue_per_type
FROM (
      /* same derived list of delivered orders with extras */
      SELECT o."order_id", o."pizza_id", COALESCE(e.total_extras,0) AS total_extras
      FROM (
            SELECT d."order_id", c."pizza_id"
            FROM "pizza_clean_runner_orders" d
            JOIN "pizza_clean_customer_orders" c
              ON d."order_id" = c."order_id"
            WHERE d."cancellation" IS NULL
           ) AS o
      LEFT JOIN (
                  SELECT "order_id",
                         SUM("extras_count") AS total_extras
                  FROM "pizza_get_extras"
                  GROUP BY "order_id"
                ) AS e
        ON o."order_id" = e."order_id"
     )
GROUP BY pizza_id
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. FINAL ANSWER: total income earned by Pizza Runner
SELECT
  SUM(
      CASE WHEN cc."pizza_id" = 1 THEN 12           -- Meat Lovers
           WHEN cc."pizza_id" = 2 THEN 10           -- Vegetarian
      END
      + COALESCE(ex.total_extras,0)                 -- $1 per extra topping
     ) AS total_income
FROM "pizza_clean_runner_orders" AS pr
JOIN "pizza_clean_customer_orders" AS cc
     ON pr."order_id" = cc."order_id"
LEFT JOIN (
            SELECT "order_id",
                   SUM("extras_count") AS total_extras
            FROM "pizza_get_extras"
            GROUP BY "order_id"
          ) AS ex
     ON cc."order_id" = ex."order_id"
WHERE pr."cancellation" IS NULL
  AND cc."pizza_id" IN (1,2);
```

